   ],
   "claims": [
    [
     "c1",
     "Identify connections from the nodes: series elements share a junction with no branch; parallel elements connect to the same two nodes."
    ],
    [
     "c2",
     "Their equivalent resistance is the sum of their resistances, and their voltage drops add to the voltage across the group."
    ],
    [
     "c3",
     "The reciprocal of their equivalent resistance is the sum of the reciprocals of their resistances, and their branch currents add to the current entering the group."
    ],
    [
     "c4",
     "Replace an identifiable series or parallel group with its equivalent resistance; repeat to find the total resistance. Use Ohm’s law to find the total current, then work backward to find group voltages and branch currents. Check that currents balance at junctions and voltage changes balance around loops."
