    {
     "id": "explainCouple",
     "targetIds": [
      "leftForce",
      "rightForce"
     ],
     "narration": "The opposite forces form a couple: the net magnetic force is zero, but the loop can turn."
    },
    {
     "id": "explainTorque",
     "targetIds": [
      "loop",
      "field"
     ],
     "narration": "For N turns, current I, area A, and field magnitude B, τ = NIAB sin θ, where θ is the angle between the loop’s normal and the field. Equivalently, vector torque is μ × B, with μ = NIA n̂. The torque tends to align μ with B; it is zero for parallel or antiparallel alignment and greatest when they are perpendicular."
    }
